{"content":[{"c":["ASHTEROTH-KARNAIM"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["City where a coalition of four kings led by Chedorlaomer, king of Elam, defeated the tribe of Rephaim giants (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.14.5","r":"Gen.14.5","rawR":"Gen.14.5","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.14.5","value":"Gen.14.5"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 14:5"},"; cf. ",{"href":"?bref=Deut.3.11","r":"Deut.3.11","rawR":"Deut.3.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.3.11","value":"Deut.3.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 3:11"},"). The area was part of the inheritance given to Abraham and his descendants by the Lord (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.15.18-20","r":"Gen.15.18-20","rawR":"Gen.15.18-20","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.15.18-20","value":"Gen.15.18-20"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 15:18-20"},"). It is probably identifiable with Ashtaroth. ",{"c":["See"],"sourceClass":"ital","t":"span"}," ",{"href":"?item=AshtarothAshterathite_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","id":"AshtarothAshterathite_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","rawId":"AshtarothAshterathite_Article_TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","t":"link","v":"Ashtaroth, Ashterathite"},"."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"AshterothKarnaim","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 14:5","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.14.5","rawQueryValue":"Gen.14.5","sourceRefExact":"Gen.14.5"},{"anchorText":"Dt 3:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.3.11","rawQueryValue":"Deut.3.11","sourceRefExact":"Deut.3.11"},{"anchorText":"Gn 15:18-20","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.15.18-20","rawQueryValue":"Gen.15.18-20","sourceRefExact":"Gen.15.18-20"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"06b0a0b3ea5ff7a4a466c65bca3ab4239dd115ea6c773cb86b49fda0024039da","sourceItemName":"AshterothKarnaim","sourceItemOrder":551,"source